<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shehu Alimi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shehu Alimi was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> Muslim cleric whose preaching drew followers in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> in the early 19th century. Around 1817 the rebel commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonja">Afonja</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilorin">Ilorin</a> enlisted him and his Muslim fighters against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaafin">Alaafin</a> of Oyo. After Afonja was killed by his former allies in the 1820s, Alimi's son Abdulsalami became the first emir of Ilorin, which joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>.</p></div>
